  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;be a solution curve of the differential equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></math>. If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then</p>"
